{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YRoa44QUmsNmWagHYHur7b","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[package]\n2\tname = \"DeepSeekCustom\"\n3\tversion = \"0.1.0\"\n4\tedition = \"2024\"\n5\t\n6\t[dependencies]\n7\ttokio = { version = \"1\", features = [\"full\"] }\n8\treqwest = { version = \"0.12\", features = [\"json\", \"stream\"] }\n9\tserde = { version = \"1\", features = [\"derive\"] }\n10\tserde_json = \"1\"\n11\tserde_yaml = \"0.9\"\n12\teframe = \"0.31\"\n13\tcolor-eyre = \"0.6\"\n14\ttracing = \"0.1\"\n15\ttracing-subscriber = { version = \"0.3\", features = [\"env-filter\"] }\n16\tthiserror = \"1\"\n17\tasync-trait = \"0.1\"\n18\tfutures = \"0.3\"\n19\tbytes = \"1\"\n20\tegui_commonmark = \"0.20\"\n21\tcpal = \"0.15\"\n22\t# GPU build attempted 2026-08-03 and reverted, both backends blocked at the\n23\t# machine level rather than in this crate:\n24\t# - features = [\"cuda\"] builds via a Visual Studio CMake generator, which\n25\t#   needs the CUDA Toolkit's \"CUDA 13.0.props/.targets\" MSBuild integration\n26\t#   files copied into VS's own\n27\t#   \"MSBuild/Microsoft/VC/v170/BuildCustomizations\" directory. The Toolkit\n28\t#   ships them under its own \"extras/visual_studio_integration\" folder but\n29\t#   they were never installed into VS, so CMake fails at the enable_language\n30\t#   (CUDA) step with \"No CUDA toolset found\". Fixing this means writing into\n31\t#   the system-wide VS install, outside this repo.\n32\t# - features = [\"vulkan\"] needs the Vulkan SDK (VULKAN_SDK env var and its\n33\t#   headers/libs), not just the GPU driver's runtime loader. Only the\n34\t#   runtime (vulkaninfo.exe) is present here; the SDK is not installed.\n35\t# Either is a real fix once the SDK/integration is installed, and\n36\t# WhisperContext Parameters already asks for the GPU unconditionally\n37\t# (see src/voice/stt.rs), so re-adding one of these features later is the\n38\t# whole change needed.\n39\twhisper-rs = \"0.16\"\n40\tkokoro-en = \"0.1.4\"\n41\t# kokoro-en 0.1.4 asks for ort \"2.0.0-rc.11\", which lets the resolver pick\n42\t# rc.13. Its source uses ort::execution_providers::CUDAExecutionProvider, gone\n43\t# in rc.13, and rc.11 moved ort::value::TensorElementType. rc.12 is the only\n44\t# release it compiles against, per its own vendored lockfile. Exact pin so a\n45\t# plain `cargo update` cannot break the build.\n46\tort = \"=2.0.0-rc.12\"\n47\t# Windows loader API (SetDefaultDllDirectories, AddDllDirectory,\n48\t# LoadLibraryExW) so CUDA runtime DLL discovery in src/voice/cuda_dlls.rs\n49\t# does not depend on PATH. Version pinned to match what was already resolved\n50\t# transitively (see Cargo.lock) so this does not pull a second copy.\n51\twindows = { version = \"=0.58.0\", features = [\"Win32_Foundation\", \"Win32_System_LibraryLoader\"] }\n52\t\n53\t# whisper-rs-sys's build.rs picks its native CMake config from\n54\t# `cfg!(debug_assertions)` as seen by the build SCRIPT itself: true means it\n55\t# defines CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=RelWithDebInfo and adds an unconditional\n56\t# -DWHISPER_DEBUG to CXXFLAGS. On a Visual Studio (multi-config) generator,\n57\t# CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE is ignored for compilation; the cmake crate's own\n58\t# `Config::profile(\"Release\")` call (hardcoded by whisper-rs-sys) picks\n59\t# `--config Release` regardless. So the RelWithDebInfo flags never apply, but\n60\t# the unconditional -DWHISPER_DEBUG still does, landing in an optimized\n61\t# Release build with WHISPER_DEBUG defined - a combination upstream\n62\t# whisper.cpp does not build or test, and which corrupts model loading on\n63\t# this machine (hangs, or aborts with CRT exit code 3, depending on run).\n64\t# Forcing debug-assertions off for build scripts makes whisper-rs-sys take\n65\t# its `else` branch (CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release, no WHISPER_DEBUG), matching\n66\t# the release profile's native build exactly. See src/voice/stt.rs tests.\n67\t[profile.dev.build-override]\n68\tdebug-assertions = false\n69\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"67ba01e2-ef71-4749-82a6-994ae563a8e9","uuid":"64471733-9d98-48e2-a48b-c60c51fbc070","timestamp":"2026-08-03T13:59:26.283Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\siriu\\RustroverProjects\\DeepSeekCustom\\Cargo.toml","content":"[package]\nname = \"DeepSeekCustom\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\nedition = \"2024\"\n\n[dependencies]\ntokio = { version = \"1\", features = [\"full\"] }\nreqwest = { version = \"0.12\", features = [\"json\", \"stream\"] }\nserde = { version = \"1\", features = [\"derive\"] }\nserde_json = \"1\"\nserde_yaml = \"0.9\"\neframe = \"0.31\"\ncolor-eyre = \"0.6\"\ntracing = \"0.1\"\ntracing-subscriber = { version = \"0.3\", features = [\"env-filter\"] }\nthiserror = \"1\"\nasync-trait = \"0.1\"\nfutures = \"0.3\"\nbytes = \"1\"\negui_commonmark = \"0.20\"\ncpal = \"0.15\"\n# GPU build attempted 2026-08-03 and reverted, both backends blocked at the\n# machine level rather than in this crate:\n# - features = [\"cuda\"] builds via a Visual Studio CMake generator, which\n#   needs the CUDA Toolkit's \"CUDA 13.0.props/.targets\" MSBuild integration\n#   files copied into VS's own\n#   \"MSBuild/Microsoft/VC/v170/BuildCustomizations\" directory. The Toolkit\n#   ships them under its own \"extras/visual_studio_integration\" folder but\n#   they were never installed into VS, so CMake fails at the enable_language\n#   (CUDA) step with \"No CUDA toolset found\". Fixing this means writing into\n#   the system-wide VS install, outside this repo.\n# - features = [\"vulkan\"] needs the Vulkan SDK (VULKAN_SDK env var and its\n#   headers/libs), not just the GPU driver's runtime loader. Only the\n#   runtime (vulkaninfo.exe) is present here; the SDK is not installed.\n# Either is a real fix once the SDK/integration is installed, and\n# WhisperContext Parameters already asks for the GPU unconditionally\n# (see src/voice/stt.rs), so re-adding one of these features later is the\n# whole chang